f-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025, on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids. November to December came in under 90% of normal in 40 of those years, more than any other pair, and in 2025 it came in at 31%. June to July ran 152% in 2025, and May to June stands at 121% so far in 2026. Grid 21137 had its driest year in 1963 at 50%.</p>"}
